<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20566" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hēro</span></b> , ūs, f.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἡρώ</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A priestess of Aphrodite</i>, <i>in
				Sestos</i>, <i>beloved by Leander of Abydos</i>,
				<i>who repeatedly swam to her across the
			Hellespont</i>, <i>but at length was drowned</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Ov. H.
			18</span></i> and 19; <i><span class="en">id. Am. 2, 16,
			31</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Deriv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hērōus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Hero</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">turres,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					9, 955</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>One of the Danaïdes</i>, <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
				170</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A daughter of Priam</i>, <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
				90</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
